    "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-app-decides-when-dom-28": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-app-decides-when-dom-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The app decides when domain-level events occur; the event protocol gives them a portable shape. App code builds events with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "@agent-kernel/protocol",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " factories (identity first, as a single "
        },
        {
          "insert": "ids",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " object inside a run scope, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "currentTraceIds()",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") and submits them through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kernel.traceWriter",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Host-defined events use "
        },
        {
          "insert": "createAppEvent(\"app:…\", ids, eventData)",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "; the factory rejects a type without the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "app:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " prefix. Runtime events (messages, tools, turns, usage) are emitted by the kernel's in-process emitter automatically; the adapter never synthesizes those."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-transcript-recovery-29": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-transcript-recovery-29",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Transcript Recovery"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-primary-trace-path-i-30": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-primary-trace-path-i-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The primary trace path is in-process emission. There is no tailer daemon. The kernel's transcript-recovery module ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "@agent-kernel/kernel/transcript-recovery",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") is a recovery tool, not a running process: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "runBackfill",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " re-imports Pi JSONL transcripts idempotently after a crash, or imports sessions that ran outside the kernel. Marker custom types are configurable where compatibility names are needed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-read-api-and-viewer-31": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-read-api-and-viewer-31",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Read API And Viewer"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-kernel-instance-ship-32": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-kernel-instance-ship-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Kernel read and catalog routes mount as the boot sequence shows. Product routes stay separate. Product routes may join app workflow state, while kernel read routes return viewer-core DTOs."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-base-viewer-path-is-33": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-base-viewer-path-is-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Viewer Model",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/40-viewer-model",
              "label": "Viewer Model"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " covers the viewer side: hosts mount "
        },
        {
          "insert": "KernelTraceWorkspace",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "AgentCatalogViewer",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and extend them only through its host seams. The host app owns surrounding navigation, headers, filters, and workflow panels. Generic trace-tree behavior belongs in viewer packages, domain interpretation in the host app."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-model-access-the-models-34": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-model-access-the-models-34",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Model Access: The Models Process, Not Auth"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-kernels-do-not-use-inter-35": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-kernels-do-not-use-inter-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Kernels do not use interactive provider auth. Every kernel points at the local "
        },
        {
          "insert": "models process",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (a proxy/load-balancer endpoint that owns the real provider credentials) through a custom provider in the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "piAgentDir",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "models.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ":"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-json-36": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-json-36",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {
        "language": "json"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "{\n  \"providers\": {\n    \"codex-lb\": {\n      \"baseUrl\": \"http://127.0.0.1:2455/backend-api/codex\",\n      \"api\": \"openai-responses\",\n      \"apiKey\": \"<local proxy token>\",\n      \"models\": [{ \"id\": \"gpt-5.5\", \"reasoning\": true, \"input\": [\"text\", \"image\"] }]\n    }\n  }\n}"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-auth-json-in-the-piag-37": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-auth-json-in-the-piag-37",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "auth.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "piAgentDir",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " stays an empty object: no "
        },
        {
          "insert": "/login",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " flow, no provider keys on disk in any kernel."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-apikey-is-a-token-38": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-apikey-is-a-token-38",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apiKey",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is a token for the local proxy, not an upstream secret. The proxy holds upstream credentials in one place for all kernels."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-agent-manifests-and-kern-39": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-agent-manifests-and-kern-39",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Agent manifests and kernel "
        },
        {
          "insert": "models.aliases",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " resolve to model ids served by the proxy provider, so retargeting a fleet is one config edit."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-kernels-stay-headless-sa-40": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-kernels-stay-headless-sa-40",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Kernels stay headless-safe (no interactive auth on boot) and model routing is observable at a single endpoint."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-examples-simple-researc-41": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-examples-simple-researc-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "examples/simple-research-kernel/.pi-agent/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the reference shape: a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "codex-lb",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " provider in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "models.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", an empty "
        },
        {
          "insert": "auth.json",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-boundary-as-a-contra-42": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-boundary-as-a-contra-42",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The Boundary As A Contract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-adapter-boundary-is-43": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-the-adapter-boundary-is-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The adapter boundary is testable, not conventional. Beyond the package-dependency direction (enforced structurally, see the implementation entries), a host app's checks should assert the behavioral half: trace writes carry container ids, subagents carry parent tool-use ids, custom loaders live in the app, and viewer pages consume viewer-core DTOs rather than database schema."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-app-adapter-model-spectre-reference-mappin-44": {
      "id": "b-50-app-adapter-model-spectre-reference-mappin-44",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Reference Adapters"
